{"id": 568, "name": "Covert Township Park", "read": "2026-10-15", "pages": [{"url": "https://covertpark.com/", "lines": ["urs of 8am-8pm everyday of the week. Our Beach Season is April 17th through October 15th. Covert Residents have free access to use the Covert Park Beach & Campground with showing an ID at entry. | One Day Beach Access | $15 We offer day passes for beach access which includes a parking spot in our parking lot. Our public beach access is every day, 8am-8pm. No dogs are allowed on the beach, we ask that visitors leave f", "cle for day use. Upon arrival please come into our Camp Store to purchase a day pass and we will guide you to parking. If we are at max capacity for the day we will put you on a call list. | Seasonal Pass Non-Resident | $50 Daily Pass Covert Resident (with proof of residency) | FREE Camping | Our campsites all have access to our beach & amenities. Each campsite is unique, offering fire pits & picnic tables. We offer ", "have access to our beach & amenities. Each campsite is unique, offering fire pits & picnic tables. We offer Developed & Primitive Sites. See our map below for an aerial view of our campsites. | Primitive Tent Campsite | $42 Our primitive sites are tucked in the forest upon first entry into the park. They are up on a hill that offers a walking path down to the large loop. Access to the shower house, pavilion, & beach ", "fer a picnic table and a fire pit, but do not offer electric or water hookup. When reserving a primitive tent site, the label on our map is a tent and the sites are T1-T7 & T10, T11, & T12. | Holiday Rates : Primitive | $47 Primitive Group Campsite | $110 Our Group Site is a primitive campsite in our dunes. This site has a limit of 18 people and 6 tents. plenty of privacy with wooded trail that leads to camp store or", " campsite in our dunes. This site has a limit of 18 people and 6 tents. plenty of privacy with wooded trail that leads to camp store or trails down to the larger loop & pavilion. | Premier Primitive Dune Tent Campsite | $50 Two of our camp sites, T8 & T9 are our premier primitive tent sites. They are located at the top of our staircase in the forest. There is parking available for these two sites in our lot. Be prepa", "amp site that is located on the top of our dunes. The campsite is located off of one of the main trails for visitors to use to access the beach, while offering it's own privacy. | Holiday Rates: Premier Primitive Dune | $55 Developed Campsite (Electric & Water) | $50 Our developed sites offer electric & a water spout. Bring your own hose please. Each campsite offers its own unique natural beauty nestled in the forest", " Bring your own hose please. Each campsite offers its own unique natural beauty nestled in the forest or up against the dunes. Each site also offers a picnic table and fire ring. | Developed RV Site (Electric & Water) | $50 Each RV site offers electric and water. Each campsite on our reservation system lists specifics for amp wattage & size of RV that will fit. A picnic table and fire pit are available at every site.", "ing online, photos of each site are posted for you to see for positioning your RV upon arrival. Call our Park Managers if you have questions about which campsite to choose for your RV. | Holiday Rates : Developed & RV | $60 Cancellation Fee: 7 or more days prior to arrival date | $10 Extra Vehicle | $10 Daily Pet Fee per pet (2 pets max per site) | $3 Cabins | We offer four cabins in our campground. There is a two ni", "questions about which campsite to choose for your RV. | Holiday Rates : Developed & RV | $60 Cancellation Fee: 7 or more days prior to arrival date | $10 Extra Vehicle | $10 Daily Pet Fee per pet (2 pets max per site) | $3 Cabins | We offer four cabins in our campground. There is a two night minimum stay. | Cabin Rental | $80 One room cabin nestled in the forest on our loops, provides electric, full size bed & twin b", "& twin bunk bed. Sleeps up to 4. Table, bench, ceiling fan, picnic table, and fire pit. There are hooks to hang items, a broom, trash can, and fire extinguisher. 6 cabins available for renting. | Holiday Rates : Cabin | $90 Explore the Western Coast of Lake Michigan | Nearby Attractions | South Haven Farm Market Van Buren State Park Roadside Beach Park Access - Dog Beach DeGrandchamp Blueberry & Cranberry Farms Saret", "k our \"Book Now\" links beginning January 1st, at 12:01am. We appreciate your patience as we transition to the online portal being the direct way to book. We do have a maximum stay of 14 days for reservations. There is a $10 fee when reserving online. Payment is made in full at time of booking. | What are the check-in and check-out times at Covert Park Beach & Campground? Check-in time is at 3:00 PM, and check-out tim", "ge by the Covert Township Board. | Are pets allowed at Covert Park Beach & Campground? Yes, pets are allowed at our campground. However, they must be kept on a leash and cleaned up after. As of the 2024 season, there is $3 pet fee per day in compliance with the Township ordinance. | Is there a minimum and maximum stay limit at Covert Park Beach & Campground? Yes, the minimum stay is 2 nights and the maximum stay is 1"]}, {"url": "https://coverttwp.com/park-beach-campground/", "lines": [" cabins, as well as primitive and developed RV sites for campers May 15 – October 15. Visit their web site for more information on rates, rules & regulations, campground availability, and more. | Covert Township Awarded $475K for North Boardwalk Improvement Project via Michigan Spark Grant Program. View Press Release | Covert Township Awarded $300,000 for South Boardwalk Improvement Project via 2023 MDNRTF Program | ", "on on rates, rules & regulations, campground availability, and more. | Covert Township Awarded $475K for North Boardwalk Improvement Project via Michigan Spark Grant Program. View Press Release | Covert Township Awarded $300,000 for South Boardwalk Improvement Project via 2023 MDNRTF Program | Management | Township park management and improvements are advised by the Covert Park Advisory Committee , who makes recommen", "ion of a pavilion are scheduled to be installed by the end of 2024 thanks to an award through the MEDC’s Revitalization and Placemaking Grant, and dollars received from the American Rescue Act. | Covert Township Awarded $146,462 for Development of Covert Community Park via the MEDC’s Revitalization and Placemaking (RAP) Program | Gallery | Click here to see Order Form | Upcoming Events | No posts found! | Recent Face"]}, {"url": "https://coverttwp.com/supervisor/", "lines": [], "via": "Supervisor"}, {"url": "https://coverttwp.com/senior-services/", "lines": [], "via": "Senior Services"}]}
